<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE - Khong Guan suffers losses.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Khong Guan suffers losses.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to April 30, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss			 (loss) 1.04  vs   1.06 (gain)</p>
<p>Dividend (cts)			  2.96  vs   2.80</p>
<p>    Group shr (cts)		     (11.59) vs  11.82</p>
<p>    Turnover				 89.69  vs  92.60</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 0.80  vs   0.55</p>
<p>    Interest expense			0.04  vs   0.01</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortisation     0.19  vs   0.12</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			  (loss) 1.00  vs   0.55 (gain)</p>
<p>    Associates				0.27  vs   0.97</p>
<p>    Tax					 0.81  vs   0.43</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries			 1.37  vs   2.47</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:    December 12, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open:  November 25, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Biscuit maker Khong Guan Flour Milling Limited said earnings  were affected by the adverse performance of its subsidiary, Beow Guan  Enterprises Pte Ltd.(BGE). BGE made a loss of S$3.69 million trading  in cocoa beans and related products, partly due to the misjudgement  of market conditions by its managing director.</p>
<p>The group said it expects the difficult operating conditions to continue  in the current year due to higher financial expenses and high cocoa  bean prices.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703093)</p>
